# Test: a stop that arrives while the boot record still holds the store waits
#       for the record, says so, and only then reports that ze stopped.
# Exercises: SIGTERM after "Ze running." -> the ordered stop in runYANGConfig
#            (cmd/ze/hub/main.go) -> awaitBootRecordAtStop
#            (cmd/ze/hub/config_source.go) -> "Ze stopped.".
# VALIDATES: spec-boot-record-after-listen, the stop fix of 322fc9e5c7: the
#            waiting line is printed before "Ze stopped.", and after the exit
#            the store's active pointer names the configuration ze booted from.
# PREVENTS:  "Ze stopped." printed while the store still names the previous
#            configuration: the call removed from main.go, or moved after the
#            line, leaves the stdout pattern below unmatched.
#
# The fixture starts ze, relays its stdout and sends SIGTERM once ze prints
# "Ze running.", which runYANGConfig prints after bootRecord.Start, so the stop
# always finds the record in flight. ze.test.boot.record.hold (test DUT builds
# only, register_boot_record_hold_zetest.go) keeps the record on the store's
# write lock for 6s, far longer than the stop's own teardown takes. The budget
# is 90s, as explicit-file-restart.ci carries for the same exposure: startup and
# the record's own syncs share the disk, which another writer stretched to 35s
# for the syncs alone (spec-boot-record-after-listen, "Shutdown overrun
# traced"), and one green run at load 21 took 52.7s. The assertions check line
# order, so a longer budget hides no failure: a red run fails on the pattern.

option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ze.test.boot.record.hold:value=6s

tmpfs=boot-hold.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
# stop-waits-for-boot-record marker
environment {
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture hub/stop-during-boot-record boot-hold.conf term 0:timeout=90s:exit=0
expect=stderr:contains=stop-boot-record: sent terminated after "Ze running."
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)Stopping: the store is still recording the boot configuration[^\n]*\n.*Ze stopped\.
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
reject=stderr:pattern=forced exit
expect=key:path=meta/config/boot-hold.conf/active:exists=true
expect=key:glob=object/*:contains=stop-waits-for-boot-record marker
